    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aeb7d9e6_2af4e7b8",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 615,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-17T21:37:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Perhaps it should return NULL here?  We don\u0027t need to re-discover the failed mode most likely, so it\u0027s not really a next one to discover. \n\nAbe would know best, but I would guess perhaps the existing \"if\" check should just be \"if !\u003d NEEDED\" and then we need to hope users of said modes check their discovery status correctly.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 613,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 615,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "37e025d303380516a4474e9c0b6361e114458098",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "503210cc_30e7b49b",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 615,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-17T21:58:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Abe told me that returning the fail was one of the uses of this function. I changed the meaning so it would show success if any SVIDs were good and nothing is needing discovery\n\nMy theory is to have the following functionality for this... With the order being pertinent.\n\nIf there are no entries then it is successful.\nIf there is an entry that needs to be discovered, then return the first one so it can be discovered.\nIf everything discovered properly in the list, then it is successful.\nIf it discovered some properly and some failed, then it is successful.\nIf it fails everything then it should return an entry that fails.\n\n\nI don\u0027t know if the fail entry should be the first one located or not... Right now the change will return the last one, but that can be changed if the first is better.",
      "parentUuid": "aeb7d9e6_2af4e7b8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 613,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 615,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "37e025d303380516a4474e9c0b6361e114458098",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "052ace3d_78adf27e",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 615,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-17T22:08:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "struct svid_mode_data *pd_get_next_mode(int port,\n\t\tenum tcpm_transmit_type type)\n{\n\tstruct pd_discovery *disc \u003d pd_get_am_discovery(port, type);\n\tstruct svid_mode_data *failed_mode_data \u003d NULL;\n\tint svid_good_discovery \u003d 0;\n\tint svid_idx;\n\n\t/* Walk through all of the discovery mode entries */\n\tfor (svid_idx \u003d 0; svid_idx \u003c disc-\u003esvid_cnt; ++svid_idx) {\n\t\tstruct svid_mode_data *mode_data \u003d \u0026disc-\u003esvids[svid_idx];\n\n\t\t/* Disconvery is needed, so send this one back now */\n\t\tif (mode_data-\u003ediscovery \u003d\u003d PD_DISC_NEEDED)\n\t\t\treturn mode_data;\n\n\t\t/* Discovery already succeeded, bump the good count */\n\t\tif (mode_data-\u003ediscovery \u003d\u003d PD_DISC_COMPLETE)\n\t\t\tsvid_good_discovery++;\n\t\t/*** change this to get the first fail instead of last ***/\n\t\t/* Discovery already failed, save first fail entry found */\n\t\telse if (!failed_mode_data)\n\t\t\tfailed_mode_data \u003d mode_data;\n\t}\n\n\t/* If no good entries were located, then return last failed */\n\tif (svid_good_discovery \u003d\u003d 0)\n\t\treturn failed_mode_data;\n\n\t/* Everything in the discovery array has been handled */\n\treturn NULL;\n}",
      "parentUuid": "503210cc_30e7b49b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 613,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 615,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "37e025d303380516a4474e9c0b6361e114458098",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ddf02da6_577a1a03",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 615,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-18T17:18:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we\u0027re going to retry failed entries, then returning the first failed probably makes more sense than last.  I defer to Abe on the need or desire for retries.",
      "parentUuid": "052ace3d_78adf27e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 613,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 615,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "37e025d303380516a4474e9c0b6361e114458098",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "177ebdcc_4313e620",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 615,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-18T18:04:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re: returning NULL vs the failed entry, pd_get_modes_discovery takes NULL to mean that the modes structure was empty (and thus, discovery is trivially complete). I can\u0027t immediately think of a way to distinguish these cases if we return NULL for failed, although there might be one.\n\n\u003e If it discovered some properly and some failed, then it is successful.\nAFAICT, this is the main change to the contract of this function. As stated above, I think it is safe with existing usage.\n\nRe: which failed entry to return, right now, there is no application for probing a failed branch of the mode structure other than indicating that the whole mode discovery process has failed, so it doesn\u0027t matter which failed entry this function returns.\n\nRe: retrying, I think that would be unnecessarily complex (although I previously also thought the same thing about continuing mode discovery after failure). In the case where the partner NAKs, I don\u0027t see any reason to think it would change its mind on retry. In the case where the partner takes too long to respond but might respond in time on retry, 1) it seems like a fool\u0027s errand to go out of our way to support a flaky partner, and 2) adding extra code for this specific message sequence seems like the wrong approach to this problem. We don\u0027t retry on response timeouts in general.",
      "parentUuid": "ddf02da6_577a1a03",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 613,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 615,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "37e025d303380516a4474e9c0b6361e114458098",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
